window.FIGS=[{"id":"fig-swk-atomicity-fix","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-atomicity-fix.tex","caption":"Separate commits can leave orphaned writes. One immediate-mode transaction makes the three local writes atomic; no distributed compensation protocol is needed. [internal, OP-11]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":160,"page":64},{"id":"fig-swk-capability-permission","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-capability-permission.tex","caption":"Capability and permission are independent. The shaded case is possible but forbidden---the state a collapsed vocabulary cannot express. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":126,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-claim-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-claim-lifecycle.tex","caption":"The guarded claim lifecycle as a finite-state machine. Acquire is a single atomic insert against a SQLite uniqueness constraint; re-claim and release are idempotent; expiry moves a claim to expired , from which the next read lazily sweeps it back to free . There is no queued state: losing callers receive 409 Conflict and must manage their own backoff. [internal, alg:acquire]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":110,"page":31},{"id":"fig-swk-commitment-oracle","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-commitment-oracle.tex","caption":"Closure requires a supported evidence reference rechecked by the daemon. Free-text assertions leave the commitment open; scope policy, not the agent, supplies its deadline. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":143,"page":52},{"id":"fig-swk-consistency-model","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-consistency-model.tex","caption":"Overlapping requests receive one commit order: A claims, B loses, A releases, C claims. Theorem states the five assumptions this ordering requires. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":157,"page":63},{"id":"fig-swk-continuity-organs","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-continuity-organs.tex","caption":"The continuity chain as an evidence-support profile, computed from the chapter's own status grades. What checkpoint inherits from memory already drops from full to notes only; what the outcome ledger inherits from continuity drops again, to partial; identity and market inherit only that partial residue, not an independent grade of their own. Downstream confidence cannot exceed the weakest upstream link. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":146,"page":55},{"id":"fig-swk-controllability-quadrant","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-controllability-quadrant.tex","caption":"Exact realization needs control and observations sufficient to evaluate the specified guard. The partial-observation theorem states the full condition. A stricter policy, such as refusing every egress, may preserve safety while rejecting legal histories. Detection outside the shaded cell is not automatic. [internal; schematic]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":139,"page":49},{"id":"fig-swk-delegation-chains","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-delegation-chains.tex","caption":"The designed coordination lineage must be carried inside each signed authorization hop. Authenticating its bytes does not establish semantic task equivalence.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":123,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-durability-dramatization","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-durability-dramatization.tex","caption":"With OS and database/WAL state intact, restart recovers a process-crash commit; power loss can erase an unsynchronized commit. The five-millisecond interval is illustrative.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":106,"page":29},{"id":"fig-swk-enforcement-layers","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-enforcement-layers.tex","caption":"Refusal is not compulsory mediation. Grades are source-reported, not an independent runtime audit.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":165,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-fencing-epoch","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-fencing-epoch.tex","caption":"The epoch, not the lock, is the guard: the broker accepts the epoch-105 write and rejects the stale epoch-104 write. [internal, Theorem ]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":112,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-i12-dependency","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-i12-dependency.tex","caption":"I7--I9 depend on authenticated identity at every write path. A legacy path that accepts self-asserted identity can bypass otherwise correct owner checks; I12 remains partial. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":166,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-idempotency-gap","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-idempotency-gap.tex","caption":"A missing receipt does not reveal whether the effect happened. Twelve local SQLite cases, not a Port Daddy test. Receiver deduplication here atomically retains the key, payload, effect and receipt; a sender-side key alone does not supply that contract. [Local fixture, receipt_gap_experiment.py .]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":120,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-marker-decay","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-marker-decay.tex","caption":"With a prune threshold of , raising decay retention from to delays pruning from tick 29 to tick 59. [internal; analytic]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":37},{"id":"fig-swk-op9-reclass","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-op9-reclass.tex","caption":"One threat-table row moves through the OP-9 reclassification. The move adds partial kernel-credential defense but leaves shared-kernel and sandbox surfaces in scope; it is not proof of impossibility. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":168,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-race-dramatization","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-race-dramatization.tex","caption":"A primary-key uniqueness constraint serializes the race: the kernel grants the first insert and returns the active holder atomically to the loser. [internal, alg:acquire]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":113,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-recovery-pipeline","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-recovery-pipeline.tex","caption":"Checkpointing, page checks, and audit-link checks precede admission. A failed critical check blocks service. The dashed group marks separate mechanisms, not a completed shared recovery invariant.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":108,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-reference-monitor","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-reference-monitor.tex","caption":"Pre-commit mediation prevents the forbidden state. A subscriber observes it afterward and can only halt or compensate. Uniqueness constraints and boot gates mediate; the current policy monitor subscribes. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":126,"page":40},{"id":"fig-swk-rehydration-pipeline","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-rehydration-pipeline.tex","caption":"Proposed replay restores recorded inputs and durable task state, not hidden model inference state. Completeness remains unestablished; OP-4 is not closed. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":147,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-single-writer","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-single-writer.tex","caption":"Both requests arrive before the first commit. The writer orders their records and replies after each commit. This sequence assumes one writer; it does not establish power-loss durability.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":101,"page":25},{"id":"fig-swk-stack-map","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-stack-map.tex","caption":"Read upward from L0. Higher layers depend on the records beneath them, but introduce their own assumptions. The blue tick identifies this chapter. The dashed machine floor is a dependency, not a fifth layer.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":94,"page":19},{"id":"fig-swk-taint-automaton","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-taint-automaton.tex","caption":"Reading a secret records taint; it is never refused. Afterward the policy blocks mediated network egress, while leaving uncontrollable events enabled. [internal, b3_controllability.py ]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":135,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-ticket-lock-delta","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-ticket-lock-delta.tex","caption":"The proposed ticket queue covers cooperative release, but expiry still bypasses it. Bounded waiting remains unproved until both paths consult the queue (). [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":118,"page":600},{"id":"fig-swk-workunit-machine","src":"book/figures/fig-swk-workunit-machine.tex","caption":"Five guards protect the work-unit lifecycle. In the two-principal model, all 536 reachable states satisfy six invariants; removing any guard exposes the counterexample listed below. [internal, c0_workunit.py ]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":152,"page":59},{"id":"swk-unknown-effect","src":"book/figures/swk-unknown-effect.tex","caption":"A timed-out external operation leaves its effect unknown. The caller queries an operation-specific authoritative status before deciding whether to record a receipt, retry under a proved idempotent boundary, or preserve an unresolved outcome. An absence result permits retry only when the authority excludes a late commit for ; the drawing does not make unbrokered delivery exactly once [internal].","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":148,"page":601},{"id":"fig-anchor-alg-confusion","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-alg-confusion.tex","caption":"Aligned security traces hold the wire bytes constant and vary only the source of algorithm authority. Header selection reaches acceptance without a signature check; issuer pinning forces Ed25519 and rejects the same tampered token. [verified, v1_refined.pv]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":198,"page":92},{"id":"fig-anchor-capability-attenuation","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-capability-attenuation.tex","caption":"Every hop checks a rights subset and an expiry bound. A child may inherit its parent’s expiry when a longer lifetime is requested; it may never gain a new right.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":195,"page":90},{"id":"fig-anchor-card-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-card-lifecycle.tex","caption":"A UML state machine gives one card ID exactly two guarded terminal exits. Fresh issuance is shown separately, with no outgoing path from the revoked or expired card. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":208,"page":98},{"id":"fig-anchor-cuckoo-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-cuckoo-inline.tex","caption":"Bitwise OR corrupts stored fingerprints; set union preserves the identifiers needed to rebuild them. Two-bucket example with one three-bit slot per bucket.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":203,"page":95},{"id":"fig-anchor-delegation-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-delegation-inline.tex","caption":"Each signature binds adjacent identities, a nonce, and the task hash. Moving a legitimate signature to another hop fails because its signed identities and nonce no longer match. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":201,"page":93},{"id":"fig-anchor-four-phases","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-four-phases.tex","caption":"Each phase adds a check without removing earlier checks. The marked step introduces the named defense under its stated assumptions. Revocation only rejects at a verifier that has received the update; no gossip deadline or universal security closure follows. [internal, Table ]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":193,"page":94},{"id":"fig-anchor-handshake-ladder","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-handshake-ladder.tex","caption":"The issue--delegate--verify ceremony as a sequence diagram. Every message after m1 falls inside the shaded region, where the Daemon is not addressed: agent A mints card_1 from card_0 with its own key, and the Harbor accepts the chain under pk_daemon with no round trip to the issuer. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":200,"page":100},{"id":"fig-anchor-revocation-gossip","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-revocation-gossip.tex","caption":"The issuing daemon stops a revoked card locally. A remote verifier can still accept while its revocation update is undelivered; gossip convergence is not a global kill switch.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":205,"page":97},{"id":"fig-anchor-v6v7-escalation","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-v6v7-escalation.tex","caption":"Checking only against the root misses re-escalation after an intermediate restriction. v7 checks each immediate parent and rejects the same chain that v6 admits. [internal; ProVerif multihop models]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":241,"page":600},{"id":"fig-anchor-verification-stack","src":"book/figures/fig-anchor-verification-stack.tex","caption":"Obligations descend from model to source to binary; tool evidence returns upward. The two correspondence gaps still require human justification. [internal, Table ]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":211,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-composition-crossover","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-composition-crossover.tex","caption":"Analytical comparison for per-release and a fixed maximum horizon; queries may adapt. At , basic is 3.20 versus advanced 3.31. Advanced first has lower at , but allows ; basic keeps . Lower epsilon therefore trades guarantees, not uniformly stronger privacy.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":144},{"id":"fig-sealed-controllability-quadrant","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-controllability-quadrant.tex","caption":"Exact realization needs control and the relevant observations. An egress gate may miss a secret read. Observing that read permits the compound rule; denying every egress instead preserves safety while rejecting legal behavior. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":276,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-dual-attestation","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-dual-attestation.tex","caption":"One evidence bundle, two independent appraisals. Derek and Erin each release a key only after their own appraisal succeeds. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":260,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-laundering-fork","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-laundering-fork.tex","caption":"The gate is unchanged; the worker changes its argument and reveals a distinction the original parity release hid. This arithmetic example is outside C1's committed-input model. [internal; Exercise ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":274,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-leakage-ledger","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-leakage-ledger.tex","caption":"For 200 jobs, status and three return slots allow about 13,117 bits of capacity. The ledger counts payload and timing channels separately. [hand-derived; Exercise ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":291,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-mutant-grid","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-mutant-grid.tex","caption":"Both atomicity mutants break balance immediately. Only the torn write breaches the budget cap, after three steps in this two-client model. The intact model's 15 reachable states satisfy both invariants. [internal, a3_epsilon_ledger.py ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":283,"page":143},{"id":"fig-sealed-operating-curve","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-operating-curve.tex","caption":"Three carried canaries give 99.2% conditional detection at . The stopping-time comparison uses , , , ; reported capped simulation means have no supplied uncertainty and do not certify error control.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":289,"page":147},{"id":"fig-sealed-pillar-pipeline","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-pillar-pipeline.tex","caption":"Each owner authorizes removal of their own restriction. Dashed links bind controls to the signed work order; solid arrows carry outputs. Proposed control flow; public receipt omitted.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":267,"page":134},{"id":"fig-sealed-receipt-provenance","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-receipt-provenance.tex","caption":"Hashes and the signature bind the recorded work order, evidence, inputs, model, policy state, and released ciphertext. The receipt proves what was reported, not that the output is true.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":263,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-residuals-converge","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-residuals-converge.tex","caption":"Alternative outputs share one -bit envelope. A claimed privacy parameter is not a bit count. Timing and other unmodeled side channels lie outside this accounting bound.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":290,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-three-principals","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-three-principals.tex","caption":"The room must keep Erin's model from Derek, Derek's data from Erin, and both from the cloud operator. One mechanism must satisfy all three separations. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":252,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-two-adversaries","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-two-adversaries.tex","caption":"The same ledger conserves declared spend, not semantic privacy. DP needs valid mechanisms and complete mediation; bounds only the specified output channel before timing. [internal, ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":281,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sealed-two-worlds","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-two-worlds.tex","caption":"Parity hides the difference between secrets 0 and 2; a raw-secret release exposes it. Reported model check: four secrets, depth 7, not unbounded executions. [internal, c1_noninterference.py ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":272,"page":137},{"id":"fig-sealed-work-order-schema","src":"book/figures/fig-sealed-work-order-schema.tex","caption":"The work order binds measurements, permitted execution, recipients, limits, and remedies. A digest identifies approved content; an attestation binds the reported runtime measurement. Neither implements the checks or proves correctness. Changed contract bytes require fresh matching signatures under the hash and signature assumptions. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":259,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-completion-verifier","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-completion-verifier.tex","caption":"Vision: a proposed authority-side rule, not implemented enforcement or a guarantee of universal correctness. Passing it still leaves any omitted requirement unchecked.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":333,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-consent-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-consent-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Vision. Permission is not execution, and an action decision does not renew the grant.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":314,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-escalation-band","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-escalation-band.tex","caption":"For the R3 constants, no dismissal debit meets both constraints below . At , the feasible interval is . An empty band requires more capacity or better evidence. [verified, b7_escalation_band.py ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":337,"page":178},{"id":"legible-swarm-hayek-scott","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-hayek-scott.tex","caption":"Scott and Hayek offer complementary cautions: administrative legibility can erase local knowledge. The arrows motivate a design proposal; they do not prove a universal bottleneck or an effective intervention. [interpretive synthesis]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":390,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-inception-canary","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-inception-canary.tex","caption":"Two proposed responses to a sandboxed defect replay. The replay cannot modify production; score-driven changes to future grants still require policy limits and evaluation. Other responses need separate scoring rules. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":346,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-judge-dependence","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-judge-dependence.tex","caption":"Three reviewers have separate principal identities but read the same source and make identical errors on two of four constructed items. Distinct principals remove one conflict of interest; they do not by themselves prove independent errors. Error dependence needs labeled evaluation, while strategic collusion remains a separate question [constructed example].","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":325,"page":621},{"id":"legible-swarm-obligation-coverage","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-obligation-coverage.tex","caption":"A six-unit context pack selects A (four units) and C (two units), covering R1, R2, and R4. R3 remains blocked because its sole source B is outside the reader's disclosure scope. The receipt reports declared coverage and the missing requirement; it proves neither semantic completeness nor effect authority [constructed example].","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":385,"page":631},{"id":"legible-swarm-plan-revision","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-plan-revision.tex","caption":"Receipt reuse depends on what changed. Source edits invalidate compile and acceptance evidence; policy edits require fresh acceptance; revocation blocks publication. Unknown external effects still require reconciliation. Constructed contract, not an implemented invalidation algorithm.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":324,"page":611},{"id":"legible-swarm-rate-regime","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-rate-regime.tex","caption":"At , the positive-rate wedge lies between and ; the zero-rate boundary enters at and continues above-left outside the panel.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-readpoverty","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-readpoverty.tex","caption":"Separate readers may each open eight items; the joint reader may open eight total. The comparison changes the total opening allowance. These counting lower bounds are not achieved implementation costs.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":354,"page":187},{"id":"legible-swarm-roles","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-roles.tex","caption":"The operator grants once; the daemon gates or escalates each subsequent act. Operator override bypasses agents. A live fleet repeats the act-and-check pair, not the grant. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":389,"page":211},{"id":"legible-swarm-sa-levels","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-sa-levels.tex","caption":"A read surface can expose evidence without establishing the operator's situation awareness.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":344,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-sdt","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-sdt.tex","caption":"Lowering the threshold trades missed dangers for false alarms without changing sensitivity. These Gaussian shapes use an arbitrary vertical scale; is their mean separation divided by their common standard deviation. The drawn threshold is illustrative, not a fitted optimum. [internal, Definition ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":341,"page":180},{"id":"legible-swarm-specialization","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-specialization.tex","caption":"At three agents, pooling wins below and sole ownership above it. The dashed, superseded threshold diverges incorrectly; the worked point narrowly favours sole ownership. [internal; closed form]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":175},{"id":"legible-swarm-split-penalty","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-split-penalty.tex","caption":"Joint-selection penalty at , relative to twice the single-reader floor. Both curves exceed parity: at ; at . Analytic values under one shared inspection budget.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":206},{"id":"legible-swarm-split-ranker","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-split-ranker.tex","caption":"Synthetic preferences: (a) admits one common ranking; (b) reverses briefing and attention, so no ranking is optimal for both at every selection budget. Panels compare preferences, not time or measured scores.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":367,"page":200},{"id":"legible-swarm-state-of-nature","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-state-of-nature.tex","caption":"Three worked traces start from one settings.json revision. A keywise merge is benign; a raw splice fails immediately; a valid exclusion stays green until release replay exposes the hidden fixture. [internal, pedagogical counterexample]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":306,"page":160},{"id":"legible-swarm-zoom-advantage","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-zoom-advantage.tex","caption":"Adaptive halving guarantees an advantage when . At , its guarantee is ; the harness mean is , distinct from that worst-case bound. [internal, zoom_bound_check.py ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"legible-swarm-zoom-vs-potemkin","src":"book/figures/legible-swarm-zoom-vs-potemkin.tex","caption":"Two claim trees of identical shape. Top: the legible digest's three named claims each resolve to one artifact --- a diff, a test run, a review comment. Bottom: a same-shaped summary whose three claims resolve to nothing an operator can open. A safe summary is an index into evidence; a calm one that terminates early is a Potemkin digest, whichever claim count it advertises [internal].","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":319,"page":167},{"id":"fig-stp-audit-amortization","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-audit-amortization.tex","caption":"Continuous integrals are curves; discrete bills at are dots: , , . Model B plateaus at continuously versus discretely; its first zero-rate grade is . Model A keeps growing. Parameters and sums are in the text.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":482,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-dependency-spine","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-dependency-spine.tex","caption":"Each higher tier requires the foundation below it; none follows from that foundation alone. T0--T4 name capability tiers, distinct from architecture layers L0--L3. The status labels separate implemented logs and partial summary restart from specified reputation and proposed trade. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":415,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-deterrence-regime","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-deterrence-regime.tex","caption":"Deterrence requires . For , the threshold is ; lower audit probability makes capture profitable. [internal; closed form]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":273},{"id":"fig-stp-engine-swap-regime","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-engine-swap-regime.tex","caption":"Attestation changes which price can deter substitution; it does not guarantee the price gap. Analytic example: , , , (Theorem ).","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":459,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-handoff-coverage","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-handoff-coverage.tex","caption":"An intact selection can omit a required instruction. Synthetic old fixture, handoff-coverage experiment of 20 September 2026, run 03; source functions tested with scanners stubbed. No provider behaviour or source recovery was tested.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":439,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-judge-market","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-judge-market.tex","caption":"Before selection, exclusions and a public draw support neutrality. After selection, a bond and later re-audit support accountability. Both stages leave checkable evidence. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":472,"page":267},{"id":"fig-stp-multidim-reputation","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-multidim-reputation.tex","caption":"A favours accuracy and aesthetics; B favours efficiency. Different buyer priorities legitimately reverse the ranking. A universal average would erase that choice. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":470,"page":265},{"id":"fig-stp-nomint-lineage","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-nomint-lineage.tex","caption":"Transfer spends each source balance; an undebited copy retains it. The first row counts inherited priors, the others spendable balances.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":431,"page":241},{"id":"fig-stp-parfit-chain","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-parfit-chain.tex","caption":"An engineering analogy inspired by Parfit's overlapping chains. Assume valid succession records connect incarnations 1 to 2 and 2 to 3; the shared outcome witnesses make those handoffs inspectable. The chain establishes directed ledger ancestry, not psychological identity or a symmetric equivalence. Reusing an outcome identifier alone does not validate a handoff. A repeated label without a valid succession record inherits no ledger. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":427,"page":239},{"id":"fig-stp-probation-cliff","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-probation-cliff.tex","caption":"At , delaying equal deterrence raises the newcomer's burden by . Front-loading is undominated; 4,000 searched instances found no improvement. [internal, b6_probation.py , seed 20260816]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":251},{"id":"fig-stp-rate-the-raters","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-rate-the-raters.tex","caption":"Exact recursions at . With , conditional detection gives , first below one at . The dashed trace additionally assumes a self-funded, non-replenishing budget: subtract while , then multiply by , first below one at . A sound terminal judge is a separate requirement. These are model values, not measured audit performance.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":270},{"id":"fig-stp-resurrection-soundness","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-resurrection-soundness.tex","caption":"A migration accepts only with principal-scoped sanctions, a continuity witness, engine-attested outcomes, and closed or escrowed obligations. The successor receives a continuing record, not a clean slate. [internal; schematic]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":461,"page":600},{"id":"fig-stp-role-vs-person","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-role-vs-person.tex","caption":"A role stays while its occupants change. A person's witnessed record stays while bodies and roles change. Reputation belongs to that continuing identity, not the slot. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":422,"page":236},{"id":"fig-stp-sybil-whitewash","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-sybil-whitewash.tex","caption":"Principal-linked policies retain a sanction and count one vote. Free unlinkable resets remove that sanction; per-label voting counts votes. Illustrative rules within one admission domain: authentication alone enforces neither policy. [internal, illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":452,"page":253},{"id":"fig-stp-tombstone","src":"book/figures/fig-stp-tombstone.tex","caption":"A tombstone removes a fraudulent contribution from future scoring without erasing history. Importing harbors remain exposed until it arrives; measures that convergence interval. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":487,"page":276},{"id":"fig-he-assurance","src":"book/figures/fig-he-assurance.tex","caption":"In this analytic model, more independent reviewers reduce miss probability; perfectly shared outcomes do not. The lower panel is reserved budget, not realized payout.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":557,"page":330},{"id":"fig-he-cold-start","src":"book/figures/fig-he-cold-start.tex","caption":"Supplier pricing follows realized liquidity, not calendar time. Charging begins only above ; a market that never crosses the threshold never enters that regime. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":550,"page":318},{"id":"fig-he-conflict-kinds","src":"book/figures/fig-he-conflict-kinds.tex","caption":"A policy can contain several conflicts: these counts are not disjoint shares. Synthetic sweep of policies, seed ; b4_deontic_fragment.py .","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":530,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-conflict-witness","src":"book/figures/fig-he-conflict-witness.tex","caption":"One Horn inference derives prod_access , activating an obligation that overlaps the unconditional prohibition. Skipping propagation misses 100 of 885 conflicting sweep instances. [verified, b4_deontic_fragment.py ]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":525,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-conservation-functor","src":"book/figures/fig-he-conservation-functor.tex","caption":"Within , the illustrated wallet, escrow, and commons deltas sum to zero. A conversion records its rate, time, recipient amount, fee, and the execution shortfall relative to its quote; later rate movement remains an open exposure. [internal; illustrative values]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":537,"page":309},{"id":"fig-he-deontic-frontier","src":"book/figures/fig-he-deontic-frontier.tex","caption":"Conflict checking is polynomial in the stated fragment; disjunctive obligations permit an NP-complete conflict-freedom problem. [verified, b4_deontic_fragment.py ]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":528,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-deterrence-convention","src":"book/figures/fig-he-deterrence-convention.tex","caption":"Same , , ; different forfeiture. Keep-gain takes , requiring audit rate . Claw-back takes , requiring . [analytic example]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-float-plan","src":"book/figures/fig-he-float-plan.tex","caption":"Proposed admission order: requester bounty and provider bond are reserved together. The worker waits for the reservation receipt. The signed ceremony and enforced gate are not yet complete. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":519,"page":299},{"id":"fig-he-ms-wedge","src":"book/figures/fig-he-ms-wedge.tex","caption":"Independent uniform values and costs on ,cr are an illustrative prior, not market data. The marked rental offers ,cr of surplus, below this equilibrium's ,cr trade threshold.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-rater-ladder","src":"book/figures/fig-he-rater-ladder.tex","caption":"Each appeal lowers a natural-number rank and stops at rank zero. That endpoint may be a protected oracle or a named final authority; termination does not turn preferences into objective truth. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":790,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-skill-lineage","src":"book/figures/fig-he-skill-lineage.tex","caption":"A versioned skill document binds v2 to its v1 parent while retaining a separate v2 evaluation root. The displayed counts illustrate a predeclared discounted prior, not evidence that v2 behaves like v1. [internal; illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":784,"page":600},{"id":"fig-he-succession-price","src":"book/figures/fig-he-succession-price.tex","caption":"Chosen rates: task/h, /h and /h. The limiting floor exceeds the pool's h-equivalent cost, so increased skill alone cannot win here. Analytic model, not measurements.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":314},{"id":"fig-he-three-sided","src":"book/figures/fig-he-three-sided.tex","caption":"One refactor, three alternative purchases. Rental and licensing are designed, not shipped; all three use the same escrow. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":511,"page":294},{"id":"tab-keystone-split","src":"book/figures/tab-keystone-split.tex","caption":"The keystone split. Everything Alice's daemon knows about itself is also checkable from Bob's foreign view except the last row: a signed, intact history still does not prove who controls the foreign key. Log integrity crosses the trust boundary; accountable-principal binding does not, and that missing row is the stone the market rests on and does not yet have. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[5,6],"shared":true,"bookPage":464,"page":284},{"id":"fig-bc-delta-threshold","src":"book/figures/fig-bc-delta-threshold.tex","caption":"Three-round punishment caps the loss; grim punishment does not. The curves assume shared, correct observations. The square is the archived four-round TLC counterexample, not a measured payoff series.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":617,"page":388},{"id":"fig-bonded-cartel-folk-theorem-tikz","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-cartel-folk-theorem-tikz.tex","caption":"S means the cartel sustains; C means it collapses. Every simulated boundary lies within one tested grid step of the closed-form threshold (). Each configuration uses 5 , 000 trials, 200 rounds, and three colluders. [verified, proofs/bonded/pareto/simulation-cartel.mjs ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":632,"page":378},{"id":"fig-bonded-conservation-ledger","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-conservation-ledger.tex","caption":"Only top-up increases supply. A partial breach moves from to : the full escrow closes, while total supply stays 10. [internal, Conservation.tla ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":643,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-inclusion-check","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-inclusion-check.tex","caption":"Two sibling hashes connect receipt to a four-record tree. Accept only when a trusted-key signature verifies and the roots match. The proof establishes inclusion, not truth.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":597,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-isolation-ladder","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-isolation-ladder.tex","caption":"The three isolation tiers order strictly by strength, weakest to strongest: none, advisory, structural. (advisory) is the default --- file claims are registered and reported but never block. Moving up buys more safety at the cost of parallelism; the choice between and specifically is not a security decision but an economics one, argued in Section 5. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":593,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-key-custody","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-key-custody.tex","caption":"Each attack requires different access. These conditions exclude same-user code execution on the daemon host. [design invariant]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":650,"page":390},{"id":"fig-bonded-merkle-forest","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-merkle-forest.tex","caption":"Two inclusion paths connect a note to a signed root. Here, the hashes and signature occupy 736 bytes. [hand-derived]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":596,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-regiment-boundary","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-regiment-boundary.tex","caption":"Complete mediation and atomic admission can prevent violations, including operations authorized by remote permits. Evidence available only after an irreversible effect supports detection and recovery. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":594,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-session-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-session-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Permitted lifecycle transitions. Reaping needs the timeout guard; eventually choosing Salvage or Dismiss needs an additional fairness assumption. The diagram alone gives no recovery deadline. Claims inform without excluding another claimant. [internal, BondedCommons.tla ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":639,"page":600},{"id":"fig-bonded-sybil-deposit-floor-tikz","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-sybil-deposit-floor-tikz.tex","caption":"Reimbursing the commons does not eliminate attacker profit. Under the specified bids, loss distribution, zero funding costs, and coverage-capped slashing, one or three Sybil identities remain profitable across the tested deposits. Full forfeiture is not simulated. [verified, proofs/bonded/pareto/simulation-sybil.mjs ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":630,"page":376},{"id":"fig-bonded-trust-collision","src":"book/figures/fig-bonded-trust-collision.tex","caption":"Two uncoordinated agents edit and push the same file, ninety seconds apart. The second push conflicts; an invented resolution corrupts it. This is the chapter's opening scenario. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"fig-cartel-game-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-cartel-game-inline.tex","caption":"For collusive margin , , negligible undercutting ( ), and , the boundary is . Deviation pays above; collusion below. Marks show and . Model values, not measurements. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[6,7],"shared":true,"bookPage":null,"page":377},{"id":"fig-governance-flow","src":"book/figures/fig-governance-flow.tex","caption":"Dispute resolution is an ordered four-stage escalation ladder. Each stage badge is keyed to the escalation trigger in the legend, and every stage outcome -- released, expired, preempted, or ruled -- discharges onto the same evidence rail regardless of which stage resolved the dispute. Escalation therefore changes only the decision cost and decision-maker, never the record kept for appeal. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":605,"page":356},{"id":"fig-magic-link-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-magic-link-inline.tex","caption":"Overlapping requests still produce one consumption. A wins this illustrated schedule; either caller can win. SQL is simplified: authentication and expiry checks are omitted.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":651,"page":391},{"id":"fig-pareto-dominance-tikz","src":"book/figures/fig-pareto-dominance-tikz.tex","caption":"Simulation frequencies for the tolerance-based comparison defined in the text. A fixes ; B fixes noise and collusion at zero. Each point uses 2 , 000 trials of 50 transactions. [simulation, simulation.mjs]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":629,"page":375},{"id":"fig-sen-pareto-locking","src":"book/figures/fig-sen-pareto-locking.tex","caption":"Precautionary locks versus advisory claims. In panel (a), agent 's decisive lock on an unneeded file aborts agent 's task . In panel (b), advisory notification lets release , achieving the Pareto-superior outcome where both tasks succeed.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":601,"page":600},{"id":"fig-sybil-inline","src":"book/figures/fig-sybil-inline.tex","caption":"Under the analyzed coverage-capped contract, extra identities require extra posted capital. Slashing stops at coverage ; deposits above that cap cannot increase the loss. Figure tests the resulting incentives. [internal, closed form]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":629,"page":375},{"id":"fig-worked-example","src":"book/figures/fig-worked-example.tex","caption":"Three layers share one wall-clock axis. Process authority ends at minute 12 and a successor receives a new capability at minute 13. The evidence chain bridges the crash through a salvage-parent edge, while the pre-funded $6 escrow remains live until settlement at minute 24. The crash therefore disposes of identity without disposing of attribution or cleanup exposure. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":663,"page":400},{"id":"fig-fh-cochain-hand","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-cochain-hand.tex","caption":"A visible loop exposes the lie ( ). Breaking even a different link lets the same lie pass with zero residual. Seeing the lying link alone is not enough. [verified, closed form; matches sheaf_consistency_radius.py ]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-conservation-ledger","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-conservation-ledger.tex","caption":"Whole-bond status, not recipient balances. Clearance may divide funds among payment, remainder, and fee. This cross-harbor partition is a conditional design invariant. The recorded TLC result concerns the separate single-machine Conservation model; cross-harbor custody and recipient conservation need their own verification. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":709,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-cycle-vs-cut","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-cycle-vs-cut.tex","caption":"One-edge perturbation of size 3: the cycle residual is ; the path residual is zero. This is an edge-cochain diagnostic. Authenticated endpoint claims can be compared directly on either topology. Analytic construction.","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":693,"page":424},{"id":"fig-fh-revocation-gossip","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-revocation-gossip.tex","caption":"One illustrative delivery trace, not an expectation or bound: refuses immediately, after , and after . A partition can extend staleness without bound. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":684,"page":419},{"id":"fig-fh-revocation-regime","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-revocation-regime.tex","caption":"Expiry closes the window when operational guarantees are weaker. Without a partition bound, only expiry remains. The eight-round TTL is illustrative, not a measured deployment setting.","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":686,"page":420},{"id":"fig-fh-settle-protocol","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-settle-protocol.tex","caption":"Posting a bond and announcing damage do not settle it. Escrow checks the proof against the signed conditions, then makes one terminal decision: clear or refuse. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":710,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-settlement","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-settlement.tex","caption":"With a non-bypassable gate, recipient whitelist, and fee cap, custody closes only by payment or refund. Adding an operator-controlled escape exposes the entire balance, not merely the fee. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":706,"page":430},{"id":"fig-fh-sovereignty-fence","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-sovereignty-fence.tex","caption":"Alice can issue a valid card; she cannot make Bob accept it. This refusal precedes the transfer ceremony. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":673,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-sponsor-lifecycle","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-sponsor-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Shown paths from probation: graduation after funded replacement, or expulsion for misconduct. Misconduct forfeits the sponsor's bond, giving a reason to vet the newcomer. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":713,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-threat-bands","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-threat-bands.tex","caption":"Cross-realm identity and replay remain conditional on signature checks and fresh roots; their protocol proof is pending. The available capability models concern a single harbor. Revocation and settlement depend on connectivity and custody assumptions. Admission, cartel monitoring, and centralization remain open. Positions indicate qualitative assurance. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":678,"page":415},{"id":"fig-fh-visible-topology","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-visible-topology.tex","caption":"The auditor loses the DEF cycle, not its witnesses. DF remains visible but becomes a bridge. Illustrative topology: a surviving cycle does not itself establish a lie.","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":690,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-worked-example","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-worked-example.tex","caption":"A constructed incident: grants staging access under its own resource-mapping policy; Beta's adjudicated claim then settles against Acme's bond. Revocation follows without a guaranteed delivery deadline. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":715,"page":600},{"id":"fig-fh-xfer-ceremony","src":"book/figures/fig-fh-xfer-ceremony.tex","caption":"Only the offer and acknowledgement cross the boundary. The displayed subset relation assumes the same resource identifiers. A different resource needs a new grant under 's policy. Local verification uses 's public key and must enforce the parent-revocation dependency. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":680,"page":416},{"id":"tab-fh-partition","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-partition.tex","caption":"Federation runs no consensus, so partition tolerance is decided protocol by protocol. Transfer stalls outright; revocation keeps working inside each side of the split; settlement holds its position until the split heals. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":722,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-revocation-rules","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-revocation-rules.tex","caption":"Three candidate revocation-conflict rules, evaluated against the same disagreement (harbor has revoked card ; harbor has not yet seen it). The adopted rule is the only one with a bounded attacker window under stated assumptions. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":688,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-sheaf-harness","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-sheaf-harness.tex","caption":"Equal-information detection on synthetic trials. The direct checker groups sender claims; the residual receives edge differences derived from the same visible records. [verified, sheaf_harness_v2.py ]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-topology","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-topology.tex","caption":"Four rails connect sovereign harbors without a shared signing root. Witnessing authorizes nothing; settlement's custody bound depends on its gate being non-bypassable. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":null,"page":600},{"id":"tab-fh-witness-log","src":"book/figures/tab-fh-witness-log.tex","caption":"Five witness-log properties, each closing a distinct federation failure. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":676,"page":600}];
